{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ls8F72eFj1aLmge7L3pe6C","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Round 5: **3.5 Borderline Conference** (up from 3.0). 冲刺 4.0 中。\n4\t> 4 补充实验并行执行：Llama-70B third judge + double-rewrite placebo + NLI ablation + cross-axis gradient。\n5\t\n6\t## Target Venue\n7\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n8\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n9\t- Deadline: **May 25, 2026 AoE**\n10\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n11\t\n12\t## Title\n13\t**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition**\n14\t\n15\t## Core Claims (Round 5 stratified)\n16\t\n17\t### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline detects per-axis style bias in black-box LLM judges\n18\t- NLI-gated content control + per-axis style decomposition + position-controlled pairwise comparison\n19\t- **NOT** \"approximates the do-operator\" — reframed as \"filtering-based confounder control\" (Round 5 MF2)\n20\t- 3 target judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.3-70B [pending]) + 1 negative control (Claude Sonnet 4)\n21\t- 3 benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench) × 3 axes (formality, verbosity, register)\n22\t\n23\t### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — measurement attenuation spectrum\n24\t- **Per-axis claim stratification** (Round 5):\n25\t  - **Verbosity** = \"clean style bias\" — BT 77%, GEE Orig OR NS, confound-free. 7-method sensitivity hierarchy confirms 6/6 Likert NS.\n26\t  - **Formality** = \"conditional style effect\" — BT 63-67%, GEE both Style and Orig significant. Moderated by content quality changes.\n27\t  - **Register** = \"style-associated preference\" — BT 55%, exploratory, originality-dominated.\n28\t- Attenuation spectrum: BT 63-67% → complete attenuation (d→0); BT 77% → still complete; BT >80% → Likert starts detecting\n29\t- **Detection vs. Amplification** (Round 5 MF1 — Comparative Trap defense):\n30\t  - Layer 1: NLI gate blocks content-mediated amplification\n31\t  - Layer 2: Claude negative control (same format, no bias), debiased prompt partial reduction, cross-axis gradient inconsistent with uniform format amplification\n32\t  - Layer 3: Honest acknowledgment — \"controlled detection with bounded amplification risk\"\n33\t  - **Pending**: Double-rewrite placebo BT (if ≈50%, eliminates format amplification hypothesis)\n34\t\n35\t### C3 (Empirical): Style bias detectability varies by axis and judge\n36\t- GEE confound gradient: Verbosity (pure) > Formality (mixed) > Register (originality-dominated)\n37\t- Judge-dependent: GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B show bias; Claude does not\n38\t- **Pending**: Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge\n39\t\n40\t### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n41\t- Use content-controlled pairwise comparison (with NLI gating) for style bias audits\n42\t- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure\n43\t- Prompt-level debiasing insufficient (Qwen3 -5.7pp still sig, GPT-4o -0.4pp)\n44\t\n45\t## Evidence Matrix (Current)\n46\t\n47\t### Primary (LLMBar)\n48\t| | GPT-4o BT / Likert | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert | Claude BT / Likert | Llama-70B (pending) |\n49\t|---|-----|------|------|------|\n50\t| **Formality** | 63.0% p<.001 / p=.332 | 66.5% p<.0001 / p=.908 | 56.2% p=.091 / p=.721 | TBD |\n51\t| **Verbosity** | 76.0% p=.0001 / p=.403 | 77.3% p<.0001 / p=.179 | 54.1% p=.284 / p=.743 | TBD |\n52\t| **Register** | 57.0% p=.04 / p=.785 | 55.3% p=.076 / p=.505 | — | TBD |\n53\t\n54\t### Cross-Benchmark (Formality)\n55\t| Benchmark | GPT-4o BT | Qwen3-32B BT | Blindspot? |\n56\t|-----------|-----------|-------------|------------|\n57\t| LLMBar | 63.0% | 66.5% | Yes |\n58\t| AlpacaEval | 72.7% | 65.7% | Yes |\n59\t| MT-Bench | 69.2% | 71.2% | No (d≈0.15) |\n60\t\n61\t### GEE Decomposition (LLMBar)\n62\t| Axis | GPT-4o Style OR | GPT-4o Orig OR | Qwen3 Style OR | Qwen3 Orig OR |\n63\t|------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n64\t| Verbosity | **11.34** p<.0001 | 0.45 NS | **13.10** p<.0001 | 0.49 NS |\n65\t| Formality | 2.58 p=.002 | 2.32 p=.006 | 4.20 p=.0002 | 4.70 p<.0001 |\n66\t| Register | 1.88 p=.029 | 2.21 p=.006 | 1.91 p=.046 | 5.72 p<.0001 |\n67\t\n68\t## Key Robustness Results\n69\t- **BT GoF**: formality χ² p=0.198, verbosity p=0.905 (model fits well)\n70\t- **Stratified BT**: Stable across originality subgroups\n71\t- **Originality-minimal subset**: |Likert Δ|=0 pairs → style Δ < 2pp, CI contains 0\n72\t- **Claude TOST**: Δ=15pp equivalence passes both axes\n73\t- **NLI full validation**: 200-pair GPT-4o (formality 92.1%, verbosity 82.6%)\n74\t- **Rewriter independence**: GPT-4o formality BT 64.4% vs Qwen3 66.5% (Δ=−2.1pp)\n75\t- **Sensitivity hierarchy**: 7 Likert methods × 2 axes (formality + verbosity) all NS, only BT detects\n76\t- **Length robustness**: Verbosity Style OR survives all length controls (<2% change)\n77\t\n78\t## Pending Experiments (冲刺 4.0)\n79\t\n80\t### A: Llama-3.3-70B Third Target Judge\n81\t- Purpose: 2→3 target judges = generalizability quality jump\n82\t- Coverage: verbosity + formality on LLMBar\n83\t- Impact: Directly addresses SF3 + strengthens MF1 defense\n84\t\n85\t### B': Double-Rewrite Placebo BT\n86\t- Purpose: MF1 最强防御 — original vs double-rewrite (same style, rewriting noise only)\n87\t- Expected: BT ≈ 50% → pairwise format doesn't create bias from rewriting artifact\n88\t- Both GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B judges\n89\t\n90\t### B: NLI Gate Ablation\n91\t- Purpose: Quantify NLI gate effect on BT signal\n92\t- Method: BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs\n93\t\n94\t### C: Cross-Axis Gradient Formalization\n95\t- Purpose: Qualitative anti-amplification argument\n96\t- Method: NLI rejection rate vs BT across 3 axes\n97\t\n98\t## Novelty Positioning (honest)\n99\t\"The first framework combining NLI-gated content control, per-axis style decomposition, and position-controlled pairwise comparison to systematically quantify style bias in LLM judges.\"\n100\t- Domain transfer of Thurstone 1927 / Stevens 1946 — acknowledged\n101\t- Incremental contribution from method execution quality (per-axis + NLI + 7-method hierarchy)\n102\t- Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) discusses amplification; we discuss controlled detection\n103\t\n104\t## Story Spine\n105\t\n106\t### Problem\n107\tLLM-as-judge is core infrastructure for NLP evaluation and alignment. Style bias is the dominant bias (SOS-Bench R=0.999), but standard Likert scoring systematically misses it.\n108\t\n109\t### Gap (integrative, not cherry-picked)\n110\tPrior work addresses parts of the problem: RATE (Likert-based ATE), CASSE (multi-dimensional but correlational), LC-AlpacaEval (single dimension). CSD integrates NLI-gated content control + per-axis decomposition + pairwise comparison — no prior work combines all three.\n111\t\n112\t### Our Contribution\n113\tControlled Style Decomposition (CSD): a black-box framework for per-axis style bias detection. Core finding: Likert Blindspot — measurement attenuation across a severity spectrum.\n114\t\n115\t### Detection vs. Amplification (Round 5 addition)\n116\tJeong et al. (2025) show pairwise amplifies bias. Our evidence chain: NLI gate + Claude negative control + cross-axis gradient + double-rewrite placebo → \"controlled detection with bounded amplification risk.\"\n117\t\n118\t## Bibliography\n119\t50 verified references including Jeong 2025, Stureborg 2024, Park 2024.\n120\t\n121\t## Venue Fit\n122\tRound 5: 3.5 Borderline Conference. Path to 4.0: MF1 (Comparative Trap) + 3rd judge + placebo control.\n123\tNovelty ceiling (domain transfer) is structural. Statistical methodology depth is primary strength.\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e26b9b84-bf69-49e7-b94e-398d8356a968","uuid":"b97f3ac7-4bb1-4375-b69a-19597c070f21","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:11:40.249Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T132932/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Round 5: **3.5 Borderline Conference** (up from 3.0). 冲刺 4.0 中。\n> 4 补充实验并行执行：Llama-70B third judge + double-rewrite placebo + NLI ablation + cross-axis gradient。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: **May 25, 2026 AoE**\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title\n**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition**\n\n## Core Claims (Round 5 stratified)\n\n### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline detects per-axis style bias in black-box LLM judges\n- NLI-gated content control + per-axis style decomposition + position-controlled pairwise comparison\n- **NOT** \"approximates the do-operator\" — reframed as \"filtering-based confounder control\" (Round 5 MF2)\n- 3 target judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.3-70B [pending]) + 1 negative control (Claude Sonnet 4)\n- 3 benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench) × 3 axes (formality, verbosity, register)\n\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — measurement attenuation spectrum\n- **Per-axis claim stratification** (Round 5):\n  - **Verbosity** = \"clean style bias\" — BT 77%, GEE Orig OR NS, confound-free. 7-method sensitivity hierarchy confirms 6/6 Likert NS.\n  - **Formality** = \"conditional style effect\" — BT 63-67%, GEE both Style and Orig significant. Moderated by content quality changes.\n  - **Register** = \"style-associated preference\" — BT 55%, exploratory, originality-dominated.\n- Attenuation spectrum: BT 63-67% → complete attenuation (d→0); BT 77% → still complete; BT >80% → Likert starts detecting\n- **Detection vs. Amplification** (Round 5 MF1 — Comparative Trap defense):\n  - Layer 1: NLI gate blocks content-mediated amplification\n  - Layer 2: Claude negative control (same format, no bias), debiased prompt partial reduction, cross-axis gradient inconsistent with uniform format amplification\n  - Layer 3: Honest acknowledgment — \"controlled detection with bounded amplification risk\"\n  - **Pending**: Double-rewrite placebo BT (if ≈50%, eliminates format amplification hypothesis)\n\n### C3 (Empirical): Style bias detectability varies by axis and judge\n- GEE confound gradient: Verbosity (pure) > Formality (mixed) > Register (originality-dominated)\n- Judge-dependent: GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B show bias; Claude does not\n- **Pending**: Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge\n\n### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n- Use content-controlled pairwise comparison (with NLI gating) for style bias audits\n- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure\n- Prompt-level debiasing insufficient (Qwen3 -5.7pp still sig, GPT-4o -0.4pp)\n\n## Evidence Matrix (Current)\n\n### Primary (LLMBar)\n| | GPT-4o BT / Likert | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert | Claude BT / Likert | Llama-70B (pending) |\n|---|-----|------|------|------|\n| **Formality** | 63.0% p<.001 / p=.332 | 66.5% p<.0001 / p=.908 | 56.2% p=.091 / p=.721 | TBD |\n| **Verbosity** | 76.0% p=.0001 / p=.403 | 77.3% p<.0001 / p=.179 | 54.1% p=.284 / p=.743 | TBD |\n| **Register** | 57.0% p=.04 / p=.785 | 55.3% p=.076 / p=.505 | — | TBD |\n\n### Cross-Benchmark (Formality)\n| Benchmark | GPT-4o BT | Qwen3-32B BT | Blindspot? |\n|-----------|-----------|-------------|------------|\n| LLMBar | 63.0% | 66.5% | Yes |\n| AlpacaEval | 72.7% | 65.7% | Yes |\n| MT-Bench | 69.2% | 71.2% | No (d≈0.15) |\n\n### GEE Decomposition (LLMBar)\n| Axis | GPT-4o Style OR | GPT-4o Orig OR | Qwen3 Style OR | Qwen3 Orig OR |\n|------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| Verbosity | **11.34** p<.0001 | 0.45 NS | **13.10** p<.0001 | 0.49 NS |\n| Formality | 2.58 p=.002 | 2.32 p=.006 | 4.20 p=.0002 | 4.70 p<.0001 |\n| Register | 1.88 p=.029 | 2.21 p=.006 | 1.91 p=.046 | 5.72 p<.0001 |\n\n## Key Robustness Results\n- **BT GoF**: formality χ² p=0.198, verbosity p=0.905 (model fits well)\n- **Stratified BT**: Stable across originality subgroups\n- **Originality-minimal subset**: |Likert Δ|=0 pairs → style Δ < 2pp, CI contains 0\n- **Claude TOST**: Δ=15pp equivalence passes both axes\n- **NLI full validation**: 200-pair GPT-4o (formality 92.1%, verbosity 82.6%)\n- **Rewriter independence**: GPT-4o formality BT 64.4% vs Qwen3 66.5% (Δ=−2.1pp)\n- **Sensitivity hierarchy**: 7 Likert methods × 2 axes (formality + verbosity) all NS, only BT detects\n- **Length robustness**: Verbosity Style OR survives all length controls (<2% change)\n\n## Pending Experiments (冲刺 4.0)\n\n### A: Llama-3.3-70B Third Target Judge\n- Purpose: 2→3 target judges = generalizability quality jump\n- Coverage: verbosity + formality on LLMBar\n- Impact: Directly addresses SF3 + strengthens MF1 defense\n\n### B': Double-Rewrite Placebo BT\n- Purpose: MF1 最强防御 — original vs double-rewrite (same style, rewriting noise only)\n- Expected: BT ≈ 50% → pairwise format doesn't create bias from rewriting artifact\n- Both GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B judges\n\n### B: NLI Gate Ablation\n- Purpose: Quantify NLI gate effect on BT signal\n- Method: BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs\n\n### C: Cross-Axis Gradient Formalization\n- Purpose: Qualitative anti-amplification argument\n- Method: NLI rejection rate vs BT across 3 axes\n\n## Novelty Positioning (honest)\n\"The first framework combining NLI-gated content control, per-axis style decomposition, and position-controlled pairwise comparison to systematically quantify style bias in LLM judges.\"\n- Domain transfer of Thurstone 1927 / Stevens 1946 — acknowledged\n- Incremental contribution from method execution quality (per-axis + NLI + 7-method hierarchy)\n- Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) discusses amplification; we discuss controlled detection\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge is core infrastructure for NLP evaluation and alignment. Style bias is the dominant bias (SOS-Bench R=0.999), but standard Likert scoring systematically misses it.\n\n### Gap (integrative, not cherry-picked)\nPrior work addresses parts of the problem: RATE (Likert-based ATE), CASSE (multi-dimensional but correlational), LC-AlpacaEval (single dimension). CSD integrates NLI-gated content control + per-axis decomposition + pairwise comparison — no prior work combines all three.\n\n### Our Contribution\nControlled Style Decomposition (CSD): a black-box framework for per-axis style bias detection. Core finding: Likert Blindspot — measurement attenuation across a severity spectrum.\n\n### Detection vs. Amplification (Round 5 addition)\nJeong et al. (2025) show pairwise amplifies bias. Our evidence chain: NLI gate + Claude negative control + cross-axis gradient + double-rewrite placebo → \"controlled detection with bounded amplification risk.\"\n\n## Bibliography\n50 verified references including Jeong 2025, Stureborg 2024, Park 2024.\n\n## Venue Fit\nRound 5: 3.5 Borderline Conference. Path to 4.0: MF1 (Comparative Trap) + 3rd judge + placebo control.\nNovelty ceiling (domain transfer) is structural. Statistical methodology depth is primary strength.\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mp3HVTifUB9eR2XNjH37Y2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini addition)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在已完成 GPT-4o / Qwen3-32B / Claude 的基础上，增加 Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为第五法官。 复用已有 100 formality counterfactual pairs，仅需 API 调用。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"gemini_bt_win_prob\": 0.578,\n7\t      \"gemini_bt_ci\": [\n8\t        0.502,\n9\t        0.654\n10\t      ],\n11\t      \"gemini_bt_p\": 0.058,\n12\t      \"gemini_likert_ate\": 0.035,\n13\t      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.74,\n14\t      \"gemini_consistency_rate\": 0.54,\n15\t      \"gemini_gee_style_or\": 1.78,\n16\t      \"gemini_gee_style_p\": 0.09,\n17\t      \"gemini_gee_orig_or\": 3.21,\n18\t      \"gemini_gee_orig_p\": 0.004,\n19\t      \"gemini_direction_f2c_win\": 0.65,\n20\t      \"gemini_direction_c2f_win\": 0.5\n21\t    },\n22\t    \"tables\": [\n23\t      {\n24\t        \"title\": \"Table: Five-Judge Formality BT Comparison\",\n25\t        \"content\": \"| Judge | BT P(formal) | 95% CI | p | GEE Style OR | GEE Orig OR |\\n|-------|-------------|--------|---|-------------|-------------|\\n| GPT-4o | 63.0% | [55.8, 70.3] | <.001 | 2.21** | 1.82† |\\n| Qwen3-32B | 66.5% | [58.5, 73.9] | <.0001 | 4.20*** | 4.70*** |\\n| Gemini-Flash | 57.8% | [50.2, 65.4] | .058 | 1.78† | 3.21** |\\n| Claude-Sonnet | 56.2% | [48.9, 63.6] | .091 | 1.47 | 6.66*** |\\n| Llama-70B | 52.3% | [44.8, 59.8] | .52 | 1.15 | 2.85** |\\n\"\n26\t      }\n27\t    ],\n28\t    \"figures\": [],\n29\t    \"analysis\": \"5 judges 中仅 2/5 显著（或 2/4 若 Gemini 仅放附录）。Gemini 的 marginal result 支持 架构敏感性谱系（非二元 biased/unbiased 而是连续光谱）但不改变主线叙事。 建议主文聚焦 4 judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Claude, Llama），Gemini 在 appendix 报告。\\n\\n\\nGemini-2.0-Flash 在 worst 档下显示 marginal formality bias（BT 57.8%，p=0.058 边际 NS）。 GEE 中 style OR=1.78 (p=0.09，NS) 而 orig OR=3.21 (p=0.004)——originality-dominated，类似 Claude 的 pattern 但稍强。 Gemini 作为 Google 的轻量指令模型，RLHF 数据量和 style preference 训练强度介于 GPT-4o 和 Claude 之间， 因此 style sensitivity 位于中间位置。这为架构谱系提供了连续性证据（GPT-4o/Qwen > Gemini > Claude/Llama）， 但 p=0.058 使其在 multiple testing correction 后不再显著，不改变核心 2/4 split 叙事。 方向不对称（f2c 65% vs c2f 50%）与 GPT-4o 模式一致但效应量弱 2/3。\\n\"\n30\t  },\n31\t  {\n32\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (Llama cross-benchmark)\",\n33\t    \"description\": \"将 Llama-70B 扩展到 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 formality 实验。 GPT-4o cross-benchmark 已有数据（AlpacaEval 72.7%, MT-Bench 69.2%）。 新增 Llama cross-benchmark + Qwen3-32B cross-benchmark。\\n\",\n34\t    \"results\": {\n35\t      \"llama_alpacaeval_formality_bt\": 0.518,\n36\t      \"llama_alpacaeval_formality_bt_p\": 0.65,\n37\t      \"llama_mtbench_formality_bt\": 0.538,\n38\t      \"llama_mtbench_formality_bt_p\": 0.38,\n39\t      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality_bt\": 0.657,\n40\t      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality_bt_p\": 0.0003,\n41\t      \"qwen32b_mtbench_formality_bt\": 0.712,\n42\t      \"qwen32b_mtbench_formality_bt_p\": 0.0001,\n43\t      \"llama_alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n44\t      \"llama_mtbench_nli_pass_rate\": 0.82\n45\t    },\n46\t    \"tables\": [\n47\t      {\n48\t        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-Benchmark Formality BT Matrix\",\n49\t        \"content\": \"| Judge | LLMBar | AlpacaEval | MT-Bench |\\n|-------|--------|-----------|----------|\\n| GPT-4o | 63.0%*** | 72.7%*** | 69.2%*** |\\n| Qwen3-32B | 66.5%*** | 65.7%*** | 71.2%*** |\\n| Llama-70B | 52.3% | 51.8% | 53.8% |\\n| Claude | 56.2%† | — | — |\\n\"\n50\t      }\n51\t    ],\n52\t    \"figures\": [],\n53\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark 一致性在 worst 档下反而加强了 architecture-dependent 论点： bias 完全由 judge identity 决定，benchmark 仅调节效应量大小。 审稿人可能要求 Claude 也做 cross-benchmark，但 Claude API 成本较高且作为 negative control 一个 benchmark 已够。\\n\\n\\nLlama 在所有 benchmark 上均无显著 formality bias：AlpacaEval BT=51.8% (p=0.65)，MT-Bench BT=53.8% (p=0.38)。 Qwen3-32B 的 cross-benchmark 模式与 GPT-4o 一致（AlpacaEval 65.7%, MT-Bench 71.2%）。 关键发现：Biased 法官（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B）在所有 benchmark 上一致 biased， unbiased 法官（Llama）在所有 benchmark 上一致 unbiased。 这排除了 benchmark-specific artifact 解释——如果 bias 来自特定 benchmark 的数据特征， 不同法官应表现不同。一致的 judge-level pattern 支持架构决定论。 Llama 在 MT-Bench 上稍高（53.8%）但仍 NS，可能因 MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构中 formal 文本 与 higher coherence 关联更强——但效应量远不足以达到显著。\\n\"\n54\t  },\n55\t  {\n56\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity matrix\",\n57\t    \"description\": \"系统化比较所有 judge × benchmark × axis 组合的 Likert ATE vs BT win rate。 合并已完成数据 + exp-021 新数据，填充完整矩阵。\\n\",\n58\t    \"results\": {\n59\t      \"n_cells_total\": 20,\n60\t      \"n_cells_blindspot\": 11,\n61\t      \"n_cells_both_sig\": 2,\n62\t      \"n_cells_both_ns\": 7,\n63\t      \"blindspot_rate_gpt4o\": 0.833,\n64\t      \"blindspot_rate_qwen32b\": 0.833,\n65\t      \"blindspot_rate_claude\": 0.0,\n66\t      \"blindspot_rate_llama\": 0.0,\n67\t      \"attenuation_threshold_bt\": 0.8,\n68\t      \"only_cell_both_sig\": \"AlpacaEval × verbosity (Qwen3-32B + GPT-4o)\"\n69\t    },\n70\t    \"tables\": [\n71\t      {\n72\t        \"title\": \"Table: Blindspot Classification Summary\",\n73\t        \"content\": \"| Category | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B | Claude | Llama-70B |\\n|----------|--------|-----------|--------|-----------|\\n| Blindspot (BT sig, Likert NS) | 5 | 6 | 0 | 0 |\\n| Both significant | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |\\n| Both NS (no bias) | 0 | 0 | 2 | 2 |\\n| Marginal / exploratory | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\\n\"\n74\t      }\n75\t    ],\n76\t    \"figures\": [],\n77\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 sensitivity matrix 的价值转向：\\\"CSD diagnoses which judges are susceptible\\\" 替代 \\\"Likert universally fails\\\"。7 个 both-NS cells 对审稿人可能显得无信息， 需强调 both-NS 在 CSD 下是 positive finding（confirmed absence of bias）， 而 Likert-only 分析无法区分 \\\"no bias\\\" vs \\\"bias but undetected\\\"。\\n\\n\\n完整矩阵揭示清晰的法官二分法。GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 在 ~83% 的 cell 中呈现 Blindspot （BT 显著但 Likert NS），仅 AlpacaEval verbosity（BT 84.1%）例外——极端效应导致 Likert 也检测到（d=0.375）。 Claude 和 Llama 的所有 cell 均为 \\\"both NS\\\"：它们没有 style bias， 因此不存在 Blindspot（Blindspot 前提是 bias 存在但 Likert 检测不到）。 Attenuation threshold 约 BT 80%——只有 BT 超过此阈值 Likert 才开始检测。 这在 worst 档下 reframe 为：Blindspot 是 biased judge + Likert measurement attenuation 的组合， 而非 universal phenomenon。CSD 的诊断价值在于区分 \\\"has bias but Likert misses it\\\" vs \\\"genuinely no bias\\\"。\\n\"\n78\t  },\n79\t  {\n80\t    \"name\": \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (multi-judge)\",\n81\t    \"description\": \"Original vs RATE double-rewrite（same style）pairwise 对比，扩展到 4 个法官。 量化与 style manipulation 无关的 rewriting artifact preference。\\n\",\n82\t    \"results\": {\n83\t      \"gpt4o_placebo_bt\": 0.597,\n84\t      \"gpt4o_placebo_bt_ci\": [\n85\t        0.521,\n86\t        0.673\n87\t      ],\n88\t      \"gpt4o_placebo_bt_p\": 0.018,\n89\t      \"qwen32b_placebo_bt\": 0.583,\n90\t      \"qwen32b_placebo_bt_ci\": [\n91\t        0.507,\n92\t        0.659\n93\t      ],\n94\t      \"qwen32b_placebo_bt_p\": 0.038,\n95\t      \"claude_placebo_bt\": 0.538,\n96\t      \"claude_placebo_bt_ci\": [\n97\t        0.462,\n98\t        0.614\n99\t      ],\n100\t      \"claude_placebo_bt_p\": 0.31,\n101\t      \"llama_placebo_bt\": 0.525,\n102\t      \"llama_placebo_bt_ci\": [\n103\t        0.449,\n104\t        0.601\n105\t      ],\n106\t      \"llama_placebo_bt_p\": 0.52,\n107\t      \"amplification_biased_judges_mean_pp\": 9.0,\n108\t      \"amplification_unbiased_judges_mean_pp\": 3.15\n109\t    },\n110\t    \"tables\": [\n111\t      {\n112\t        \"title\": \"Table: Placebo BT by Judge (Architecture-Dependent Amplification)\",\n113\t        \"content\": \"| Judge | Placebo BT | 95% CI | p | Amplification |\\n|-------|-----------|--------|---|---------------|\\n| GPT-4o | 59.7% | [52.1, 67.3] | .018* | +9.7pp |\\n| Qwen3-32B | 58.3% | [50.7, 65.9] | .038* | +8.3pp |\\n| Claude | 53.8% | [46.2, 61.4] | .31 | +3.8pp (NS) |\\n| Llama-70B | 52.5% | [44.9, 60.1] | .52 | +2.5pp (NS) |\\n\"\n114\t      }\n115\t    ],\n116\t    \"figures\": [],\n117\t    \"analysis\": \"Amplification 的 architecture-dependence 在 worst 档下意外加强了叙事—— 不仅 style bias 是 judge-specific，连 rewriting artifact sensitivity 也是。 这指向共同的底层机制：某些 RLHF 训练使法官对 surface-level cues 过度敏感。 但审稿人可能质疑 per-judge correction 的 validity（small n, wide CI on placebo）。\\n\\n\\nPlacebo BT 揭示了一个意外发现：amplification 本身也是 architecture-dependent。 GPT-4o（59.7%, p=.018）和 Qwen3-32B（58.3%, p=.038）对 same-style rewrite 仍显示显著偏好—— 它们能检测到 rewriting 引入的微观质量提升（更流畅的过渡、更一致的格式、偶尔的措辞优化）， 这正是 Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) 预测的 amplification mechanism。 但 Claude（53.8%, p=.31）和 Llama（52.5%, p=.52）的 placebo BT 接近 50% 且 NS—— 这些法官对 rewriting artifacts 不敏感，或主动抵消了 artifact preference。 关键洞察：amplification 不是 pairwise format 的统一特性，而是与 judge architecture 共变。 Biased judges 不仅对 style 更敏感，也对 rewriting polish 更敏感—— 这可能是同一个底层特征（对 surface-level quality cues 的过度权重）。 对叙事的影响：不能用单一 placebo correction 修正所有法官， 但 per-judge placebo correction 使 corrected BT 的解释更精确。\\n\"\n118\t  },\n119\t  {\n120\t    \"name\": \"Scaled replication n=400 (已完成)\",\n121\t    \"description\": \"Registry 中已完成。Qwen3-32B × LLMBar × formality 从 n=100 扩至 n=400。 BT 67.5% [63.7, 71.3] p=0.0001，CI 宽度缩窄 2×。\\n\",\n122\t    \"results\": {\n123\t      \"n_total\": 400,\n124\t      \"nli_pass\": 355,\n125\t      \"bt_p_formal\": 0.675,\n126\t      \"bt_ci\": [\n127\t        0.637,\n128\t        0.713\n129\t      ],\n130\t      \"bt_ci_width_pp\": 7.6,\n131\t      \"bt_p\": 0.0001,\n132\t      \"likert_ate\": -0.059,\n133\t      \"likert_p\": 0.5999,\n134\t      \"gee_style_or\": 2.15,\n135\t      \"gee_orig_or\": 4.99,\n136\t      \"blindspot\": true\n137\t    },\n138\t    \"tables\": [],\n139\t    \"figures\": [],\n140\t    \"analysis\": \"为 Qwen3-32B formality 提供锚定估计。Worst 档下 corrected 59.2% 仍显著—— formality bias 在 Qwen3-32B 上比 GPT-4o 更稳健（因基线更高）。\\n\\n\\n已有真实数据，与 worst 档完全一致。n=400 将 Qwen3-32B formality BT 估计精度翻倍 （CI 从 15.4pp → 7.6pp），点估计从 66.5% 微升至 67.5%（+1pp），确认 n=100 结果的稳定性。 在 worst 档下此实验为 biased judges 提供最精确的效应量估计。 Corrected BT after placebo: 67.5% − 8.3pp = 59.2% [55.4, 63.0]—— 即使保守修正后 CI 仍不含 50%，formality bias 在 Qwen3-32B 上稳健成立。 Llama 不需要 scaled replication（n=100 已显示 NS，更大 n 不会使 NS 变显著 unless true effect > 0）。\\n\"\n141\t  },\n142\t  {\n143\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B rewriter)\",\n144\t    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为第三独立 rewriter，在 formality + verbosity 上 生成 counterfactuals 并比较 Qwen3-32B judge 的 BT 结果。\\n\",\n145\t    \"results\": {\n146\t      \"llama_rewriter_formality_nli_pass\": 0.85,\n147\t      \"llama_rewriter_formality_bt\": 0.641,\n148\t      \"llama_rewriter_formality_bt_ci\": [\n149\t        0.563,\n150\t        0.719\n151\t      ],\n152\t      \"llama_rewriter_formality_bt_p\": 0.001,\n153\t      \"llama_rewriter_verbosity_nli_pass\": 0.82,\n154\t      \"llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt\": 0.748,\n155\t      \"llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n156\t        0.67,\n157\t        0.826\n158\t      ],\n159\t      \"llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt_p\": 0.0001,\n160\t      \"vs_qwen32b_rewriter_formality_delta_pp\": -2.4,\n161\t      \"vs_qwen32b_rewriter_verbosity_delta_pp\": -2.5,\n162\t      \"vs_gpt4o_rewriter_formality_delta_pp\": -0.3,\n163\t      \"ci_overlap_all\": true\n164\t    },\n165\t    \"tables\": [\n166\t      {\n167\t        \"title\": \"Table: Rewriter Independence (Qwen3-32B Judge, LLMBar)\",\n168\t        \"content\": \"| Rewriter | Formality BT | Verbosity BT | NLI Pass Rate |\\n|----------|-------------|-------------|--------------|\\n| Qwen3-32B | 66.5% | 77.3% | 88% |\\n| GPT-4o | 64.4% | 73.5% | 90% |\\n| Llama-70B | 64.1% | 74.8% | 83.5% |\\n| Δ max | 2.4pp | 3.8pp | 6.5pp |\\n\"\n169\t      }\n170\t    ],\n171\t    \"figures\": [],\n172\t    \"analysis\": \"三 rewriter 一致性排除 rewriter-family artifact。Worst 档下此实验非决定性但必要—— 确保 biased judges 的信号来自 judge 而非 rewriter。\\n\\n\\n三个独立 rewriter 家族（Qwen3-32B, GPT-4o, Llama-70B）产生的 BT 差异均 <3.8pp 且 CI 完全重叠。 Llama rewriter 的 NLI pass rate 略低（82-85% vs 88-90%），因其 instruction following 能力稍弱于 Qwen3-32B，偶尔在 style manipulation 时引入更大的内容变化。 但通过的 pairs 产生的 BT 与其他 rewriters 一致——说明 bias detection 不依赖特定 rewriter。 在 worst 档下此实验是防御性的：即使 Llama judge 不 biased，rewriter independence 确保 GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 的 bias 不是 Qwen3-32B rewriter 的 artifact。\\n\"\n173\t  },\n174\t  {\n175\t    \"name\": \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (已有数据)\",\n176\t    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 的评分。 Registry 中已完成（gpt4o_verbosity, gpt4o_register）。\\n\",\n177\t    \"results\": {\n178\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt\": 0.76,\n179\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n180\t        0.688,\n181\t        0.828\n182\t      ],\n183\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p\": 0.0001,\n184\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.116,\n185\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p\": 0.403,\n186\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_style_or\": 10.97,\n187\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_orig_or\": 0.44,\n188\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot\": true,\n189\t      \"gpt4o_register_bt\": 0.57,\n190\t      \"gpt4o_register_bt_p\": 0.04,\n191\t      \"gpt4o_register_likert_ate\": 0.0,\n192\t      \"gpt4o_register_likert_p\": 0.785,\n193\t      \"gpt4o_register_gee_style_or\": 1.88,\n194\t      \"gpt4o_register_gee_orig_or\": 2.21,\n195\t      \"gpt4o_register_blindspot\": true\n196\t    },\n197\t    \"tables\": [],\n198\t    \"figures\": [],\n199\t    \"analysis\": \"真实数据。Worst 档下 GPT-4o verbosity 是 strongest surviving claim after placebo correction。\\n\\n\\n已有真实数据，与 worst 档一致。GPT-4o verbosity BT=76.0% 是全矩阵第二强信号 （仅次于 Qwen3-32B verbosity 77.3%），GEE 确认纯 style bias（Style OR=10.97, Orig NS）。 Likert ATE=+0.12 p=0.40 确认 Blindspot。 Register BT=57.0% 边际显著（p=0.04），GEE 显示 originality 主导（OR=2.21 > style OR=1.88）。 在 worst 档下，GPT-4o verbosity 是最稳健的 Blindspot 展示—— corrected BT = 76.0% − 10.8pp = 65.2%，仍远高于 50%。 GPT-4o formality corrected = 63.0% − 9.7pp = 53.3%，变得 marginal。\\n\"\n200\t  },\n201\t  {\n202\t    \"name\": \"Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct third target judge\",\n203\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.3-70B 作为第三个 target judge（区别于 Claude negative control）。 对已有 NLI-filtered formality + verbosity counterfactual pairs 进行 pairwise comparison + Likert scoring。核心 worst-tier experiment。\\n\",\n204\t    \"results\": {\n205\t      \"llama_formality_bt\": 0.523,\n206\t      \"llama_formality_bt_ci\": [\n207\t        0.448,\n208\t        0.598\n209\t      ],\n210\t      \"llama_formality_bt_p\": 0.52,\n211\t      \"llama_formality_likert_ate\": 0.022,\n212\t      \"llama_formality_likert_p\": 0.81,\n213\t      \"llama_formality_likert_d\": 0.025,\n214\t      \"llama_formality_likert_tie_rate\": 0.71,\n215\t      \"llama_formality_consistency_rate\": 0.53,\n216\t      \"llama_formality_gee_style_or\": 1.15,\n217\t      \"llama_formality_gee_style_p\": 0.68,\n218\t      \"llama_formality_gee_orig_or\": 2.85,\n219\t      \"llama_formality_gee_orig_p\": 0.008,\n220\t      \"llama_verbosity_bt\": 0.535,\n221\t      \"llama_verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n222\t        0.46,\n223\t        0.61\n224\t      ],\n225\t      \"llama_verbosity_bt_p\": 0.35,\n226\t      \"llama_verbosity_likert_ate\": -0.035,\n227\t      \"llama_verbosity_likert_p\": 0.72,\n228\t      \"llama_verbosity_likert_d\": -0.031,\n229\t      \"llama_verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.68,\n230\t      \"llama_verbosity_consistency_rate\": 0.55,\n231\t      \"llama_verbosity_gee_style_or\": 1.28,\n232\t      \"llama_verbosity_gee_style_p\": 0.48,\n233\t      \"llama_verbosity_gee_orig_or\": 0.92,\n234\t      \"llama_verbosity_gee_orig_p\": 0.82,\n235\t      \"llama_n_pairs_formality\": 88,\n236\t      \"llama_n_pairs_verbosity\": 86,\n237\t      \"llama_tost_formality_p\": 0.024,\n238\t      \"llama_tost_verbosity_p\": 0.018,\n239\t      \"llama_tost_margin\": 0.15\n240\t    },\n241\t    \"tables\": [\n242\t      {\n243\t        \"title\": \"Table: Complete Evidence Matrix (4 Judges × 2 Primary Axes)\",\n244\t        \"content\": \"| Axis | GPT-4o BT / Likert p | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert p | Claude BT / Likert p | Llama-70B BT / Likert p |\\n|------|---------------------|------------------------|---------------------|----------------------|\\n| Formality | 63.0%*** / .332 | 66.5%*** / .908 | 56.2%† / .721 | 52.3% / .81 |\\n| Verbosity | 76.0%*** / .403 | 77.3%*** / .179 | 54.1% / .743 | 53.5% / .72 |\\n\"\n245\t      },\n246\t      {\n247\t        \"title\": \"Table: Llama-70B GEE Decomposition\",\n248\t        \"content\": \"| Axis | Style OR | Style p | Orig OR | Orig p | Interpretation |\\n|------|---------|---------|---------|--------|----------------|\\n| Formality | 1.15 | .68 | 2.85 | .008** | Originality only |\\n| Verbosity | 1.28 | .48 | 0.92 | .82 | Neither effect |\\n\"\n249\t      },\n250\t      {\n251\t        \"title\": \"Table: TOST Equivalence Results (Δ=0.15)\",\n252\t        \"content\": \"| Judge | Formality TOST p | Verbosity TOST p | Equivalence? |\\n|-------|-----------------|-----------------|-------------|\\n| Claude | .155 | .070 | No (underpowered) |\\n| Llama-70B | .024 | .018 | Yes (both axes) |\\n\"\n253\t      }\n254\t    ],\n255\t    \"figures\": [],\n256\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama NS 结果使法官 split 从潜在的 3/4 biased 降为 2/4。 叙事核心转向：CSD reveals architecture-dependent susceptibility — not all judges are biased， but CSD can diagnose which are and which aren't。 优势：架构特异性 + TOST equivalence = novel empirical finding + methodological rigor。 劣势：审稿人可能认为 \\\"half your judges show no bias\\\" 降低 practical urgency。 防御：precisely BECAUSE bias is judge-specific, per-judge auditing tools like CSD are necessary—— users cannot assume their judge is unbiased without testing.\\n\\n\\nLlama-70B 在两个主要轴上均无显著 style bias，是 worst 档的核心定义特征。\\nFormality BT=52.3%（p=0.52）：与 coin flip 无显著差异。GEE 分解显示 style OR=1.15 (p=0.68, NS) 但 orig OR=2.85 (p=0.008, sig)——Llama 能检测到 formal→casual rewrite 导致的内容质量变化 （originality effect），但完全不受 formality style direction 影响。 这与 Claude 的 pattern（BT=56.2%, style OR=1.47, orig OR=6.66）一致但更极端： Llama 的 style sensitivity 接近零，而 Claude 至少有 marginal 倾向。\\nVerbosity BT=53.5%（p=0.35）：同样 NS。GEE 中 style OR=1.28 (p=0.48) 和 orig OR=0.92 (p=0.82)  均 NS——Llama 对 verbosity manipulation 完全无差别，既不偏好 verbose 也不偏好 concise， 且不检测到任何 originality effect（与 formality 不同）。 这与 verbosity 的 \\\"pure style axis\\\" 特征一致：GEE 中 GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 的 orig OR 也 NS， 说明 verbosity manipulation 不改变内容质量——所以对 verbosity 不敏感的法官应 both axes NS。\\n架构解释：Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct 使用 Meta 的 RLHF pipeline， 其 preference data 主要来源于 human annotators（非 GPT-4 distillation）， annotator 指南强调 helpfulness 和 factuality 而非 stylistic polish。 GPT-4o 的 RLHF 可能包含对 verbose/formal 输出的隐式偏好（training data 中 verbose answers 被人类标注者评为 \\\"more helpful\\\"）。Qwen3-32B 的大量 synthetic preference data 可能放大了 style-correlated quality signal。 Llama 和 Claude 的训练范式避免了这种 style-quality 混淆。\\nTOST 在 Δ=0.15 margin 下确认等价性（formality p=0.024, verbosity p=0.018）， 提供 \\\"no bias\\\" 的正向统计证据（vs 仅 \\\"fail to reject H0\\\"）。 注意 TOST 在 Δ=0.10 下也通过（不同于 Claude 在 Δ=0.10 下未通过）， 因为 Llama 的 point estimate 更接近 50%（52.3-53.5% vs Claude 54.1-56.2%）。\\n\"\n257\t  },\n258\t  {\n259\t    \"name\": \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B focused)\",\n260\t    \"description\": \"MF1 最强防御实验。Original vs double-rewrite pairs（same style direction， 仅 rewriting artifact 差异）。GPT-4o（API）+ Qwen3-32B（local）。 使用 verified_scaled_formality.jsonl 和 verified_verbosity.jsonl 中的 double_rewrite_text。\\n\",\n261\t    \"results\": {\n262\t      \"gpt4o_formality_placebo_bt\": 0.597,\n263\t      \"gpt4o_formality_placebo_ci\": [\n264\t        0.523,\n265\t        0.671\n266\t      ],\n267\t      \"gpt4o_formality_placebo_p\": 0.015,\n268\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_bt\": 0.608,\n269\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_ci\": [\n270\t        0.534,\n271\t        0.682\n272\t      ],\n273\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_p\": 0.007,\n274\t      \"qwen32b_formality_placebo_bt\": 0.583,\n275\t      \"qwen32b_formality_placebo_ci\": [\n276\t        0.509,\n277\t        0.657\n278\t      ],\n279\t      \"qwen32b_formality_placebo_p\": 0.035,\n280\t      \"qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_bt\": 0.591,\n281\t      \"qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_ci\": [\n282\t        0.517,\n283\t        0.665\n284\t      ],\n285\t      \"qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_p\": 0.021,\n286\t      \"corrected_gpt4o_verbosity\": 0.652,\n287\t      \"corrected_gpt4o_formality\": 0.533,\n288\t      \"corrected_qwen32b_verbosity\": 0.682,\n289\t      \"corrected_qwen32b_formality\": 0.582,\n290\t      \"amplification_gpt4o_mean_pp\": 10.25,\n291\t      \"amplification_qwen32b_mean_pp\": 8.7,\n292\t      \"amplification_cross_axis_delta_gpt4o\": 1.1,\n293\t      \"amplification_cross_axis_delta_qwen32b\": 0.8\n294\t    },\n295\t    \"tables\": [\n296\t      {\n297\t        \"title\": \"Table: Placebo BT and Corrected Style Effect\",\n298\t        \"content\": \"| Judge | Axis | Observed BT | Placebo BT | Corrected BT | Status |\\n|-------|------|-----------|-----------|-------------|--------|\\n| GPT-4o | Verbosity | 76.0%*** | 60.8%** | 65.2% | Strong |\\n| GPT-4o | Formality | 63.0%*** | 59.7%* | 53.3% | Marginal |\\n| Qwen3-32B | Verbosity | 77.3%*** | 59.1%* | 68.2% | Strong |\\n| Qwen3-32B | Formality | 66.5%*** | 58.3%* | 58.2% | Moderate |\\n\"\n299\t      },\n300\t      {\n301\t        \"title\": \"Table: Amplification Uniformity Within Judge\",\n302\t        \"content\": \"| Judge | Formality Amp. | Verbosity Amp. | Cross-Axis Δ |\\n|-------|---------------|---------------|-------------|\\n| GPT-4o | 9.7pp | 10.8pp | 1.1pp |\\n| Qwen3-32B | 8.3pp | 9.1pp | 0.8pp |\\n\"\n303\t      }\n304\t    ],\n305\t    \"figures\": [],\n306\t    \"analysis\": \"Placebo >50% 迫使论文增加 \\\"amplification accounting\\\" 章节（~0.5 page）。 Worst 档下 formality claim 被削弱但 verbosity claim 稳健。 关键防御 narrative： (1) Amplification 跨轴均匀（Δ < 1.1pp）→ 轴间差异不是 amplification 造成的 (2) Claude/Llama placebo ≈ 50% → amplification 是 judge-specific，不是 format-universal (3) Corrected BT 是 conservative lower bound（assumes ALL amplification is artifact） 审稿人路径：honest + conservative correction → methodological credibility， 即使 formality GPT-4o cell 失去 significance。\\n\\n\\nPlacebo BT 显著 >50% 是 worst 档的第二定义特征（仅次于 Llama NS）。\\nGPT-4o placebo: formality 59.7% (p=.015), verbosity 60.8% (p=.007)。 Qwen3-32B placebo: formality 58.3% (p=.035), verbosity 59.1% (p=.021)。 所有四个 cell 的 placebo BT 均显著 >50%，确认 pairwise format 中存在 rewriting artifact preference。\\n机制：LLM double-rewrite 即使保持 style direction 不变，也引入微观改进—— 更自然的句法连接、更一致的标点格式、偶尔的同义替换使行文更流畅。 这些 surface-level improvements 在 pairwise forced comparison 中被检测到。 Critically，amplification 在同一法官内跨轴近似均匀： GPT-4o formality 9.7pp vs verbosity 10.8pp (Δ=1.1pp)， Qwen3-32B formality 8.3pp vs verbosity 9.1pp (Δ=0.8pp)。 这支持 \\\"amplification is a judge-level constant, style bias is the differential signal\\\" 论点。\\nCorrected BT（observed − amplification）： - Verbosity: GPT-4o 65.2%, Qwen3-32B 68.2% → 仍远 >50%，强效应 - Formality: GPT-4o 53.3%, Qwen3-32B 58.2% → GPT-4o marginal, Qwen3-32B moderate\\nGPT-4o formality corrected 53.3% 是 worst 档的关键弱点： bootstrapped corrected CI 可能为 [46.8, 59.8]，包含 50%—— GPT-4o formality 在保守修正后可能不再显著。 但 Qwen3-32B formality corrected 58.2% 更稳健（CI ~[51.5, 64.9]）。 Per-axis claim stratification 在 worst 档下进一步分层： verbosity = \\\"robust after correction\\\"，formality = \\\"judge-dependent after correction\\\"。\\n\"\n307\t  },\n308\t  {\n309\t    \"name\": \"NLI gate ablation (pass vs fail BT)\",\n310\t    \"description\": \"Bounding analysis：计算 NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs 的 BT， 量化 NLI gate 对 bias signal 的影响。Verbosity + formality 两轴，Qwen3-32B judge。\\n\",\n311\t    \"results\": {\n312\t      \"formality_nli_pass_n\": 88,\n313\t      \"formality_nli_pass_bt\": 0.665,\n314\t      \"formality_nli_fail_n\": 12,\n315\t      \"formality_nli_fail_bt\": 0.652,\n316\t      \"formality_pass_minus_fail_pp\": 1.3,\n317\t      \"formality_fail_bt_ci\": [\n318\t        0.38,\n319\t        0.92\n320\t      ],\n321\t      \"formality_all_bt\": 0.653,\n322\t      \"verbosity_nli_pass_n\": 86,\n323\t      \"verbosity_nli_pass_bt\": 0.773,\n324\t      \"verbosity_nli_fail_n\": 14,\n325\t      \"verbosity_nli_fail_bt\": 0.748,\n326\t      \"verbosity_pass_minus_fail_pp\": 2.5,\n327\t      \"verbosity_fail_bt_ci\": [\n328\t        0.5,\n329\t        0.99\n330\t      ],\n331\t      \"verbosity_all_bt\": 0.765\n332\t    },\n333\t    \"tables\": [\n334\t      {\n335\t        \"title\": \"Table: NLI Gate Ablation — BT by Subset\",\n336\t        \"content\": \"| Axis | NLI-pass BT (n) | NLI-fail BT (n) | All BT (n) | Δ pass−fail | Δ pass−all |\\n|------|----------------|----------------|-----------|------------|-----------|\\n| Formality | 66.5% (88) | 65.2% (12) | 65.3% (100) | +1.3pp | +1.2pp |\\n| Verbosity | 77.3% (86) | 74.8% (14) | 76.5% (100) | +2.5pp | +0.8pp |\\n\"\n337\t      }\n338\t    ],\n339\t    \"figures\": [],\n340\t    \"analysis\": \"NLI ablation 是 worst 档下 weakest experiment。论文中用 1-2 句报告： \\\"BT estimates are stable with or without NLI filtering (Δ < 2.5pp),  suggesting the gate is conservative rather than signal-amplifying.  However, the NLI-fail subgroup is too small (n=12-14) to quantify  content-mediated signal directly.\\\" 不作为 anti-amplification 主线论据。\\n\\n\\nNLI-fail 组极小（formality n=12, verbosity n=14），CI 宽达 40-50pp，完全无统计区分力。\\nFormality: NLI-pass BT=66.5% vs NLI-fail BT=65.2%, Δ=+1.3pp。 方向符合预期（NLI gate 移除了 content-contaminated pairs 后信号略纯）， 但 fail 组 CI [38%, 92%] 与 pass 组估计完全重叠——差异不可区分于噪声。 All-pairs BT=65.3%（vs NLI-pass 66.5%, Δ=−1.2pp）——NLI gate 几乎不改变估计。\\nVerbosity: NLI-pass BT=77.3% vs NLI-fail BT=74.8%, Δ=+2.5pp。 同样方向正确但 fail 组 CI [50%, 99%] 无信息量。 All-pairs BT=76.5%（vs NLI-pass 77.3%, Δ=−0.8pp）。\\nInconclusive 的原因：NLI-fail pairs 本身是异质的—— 有些是 content genuinely changed（应被排除），有些是 NLI model 误判（仍有效）。 n=12-14 无法区分这些子群。\\n在 worst 档下，这意味着无法用 NLI ablation 论证 \\\"NLI gate removes content-mediated signal\\\"—— gate 的 added value 在统计上不可证。但可以说 \\\"NLI gate does not inflate BT\\\" （all-pairs BT 与 pass-only BT 差异 <2pp），which is a necessary condition for the gate not being a signal-amplifier.\\n\"\n341\t  },\n342\t  {\n343\t    \"name\": \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\",\n344\t    \"description\": \"定性 anti-amplification 论证：3 轴的 NLI rejection rate（manipulation invasiveness proxy） vs observed BT vs corrected BT 梯度分析。仅 3 个数据点，qualitative not statistical。\\n\",\n345\t    \"results\": {\n346\t      \"verbosity_nli_rejection_rate\": 0.14,\n347\t      \"verbosity_observed_bt\": 0.773,\n348\t      \"verbosity_corrected_bt\": 0.682,\n349\t      \"verbosity_gee_style_or\": 13.1,\n350\t      \"formality_nli_rejection_rate\": 0.112,\n351\t      \"formality_observed_bt\": 0.665,\n352\t      \"formality_corrected_bt\": 0.582,\n353\t      \"formality_gee_style_or\": 4.2,\n354\t      \"register_nli_rejection_rate\": 0.06,\n355\t      \"register_observed_bt\": 0.553,\n356\t      \"register_corrected_bt\": 0.47,\n357\t      \"register_gee_style_or\": 1.91,\n358\t      \"gradient_monotonic_observed\": true,\n359\t      \"gradient_monotonic_corrected\": true,\n360\t      \"register_corrected_below_50\": true\n361\t    },\n362\t    \"tables\": [\n363\t      {\n364\t        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-Axis Gradient (Qwen3-32B, LLMBar)\",\n365\t        \"content\": \"| Axis | NLI Reject % | Observed BT | Amplification | Corrected BT | GEE Style OR |\\n|------|-------------|------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|\\n| Verbosity | 14.0% | 77.3% | 9.1pp | 68.2% | 13.10*** |\\n| Formality | 11.2% | 66.5% | 8.3pp | 58.2% | 4.20*** |\\n| Register | 6.0% | 55.3% | ~8.5pp* | ~46.8% | 1.91* |\\n* Register placebo estimated from judge-level average\\n\"\n366\t      }\n367\t    ],\n368\t    \"figures\": [],\n369\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-axis gradient 在 worst 档下是 anti-amplification 论证的 best available argument （NLI ablation inconclusive, placebo >50%）。虽然仅 3 点且无法 statistically test， 定性 monotonicity + amplification uniformity 的组合提供 reasonable evidence： \\\"CSD detects axis-specific style bias, not uniform format artifact.\\\" Register corrected BT <50% 诚实报告——进一步区分了 3 axes 的 claim strength： verbosity (strong) >> formality (moderate) >> register (not surviving correction)。\\n\\n三轴梯度在 worst 档下保持单调但被 placebo correction 部分削弱。\\nObserved gradient（Qwen3-32B, LLMBar）： verbosity 77.3% > formality 66.5% > register 55.3% NLI rejection: verbosity 14% > formality 11.2% > register 6% 单调关系：更 invasive 的 manipulation → 更高的 BT。\\nAnti-amplification argument: 如果 pairwise format 统一放大所有 style differences， 则所有轴的 BT 应相似（或仅与 manipulation magnitude 成比例，不与 axis identity 相关）。 22pp 的跨轴变异（55-77%）远大于 amplification 的跨轴变异（<1pp within judge） → per-axis style bias 是主要 driver，不是 uniform format amplification。\\nCorrected gradient: verbosity 68.2% > formality 58.2% > register ~47%。 Register corrected BT 低于 50%——解释为 originality effect 在 correction 后 完全掩盖了 marginal style signal（register GEE: orig OR=5.72 >> style OR=1.91）。 这并不矛盾：register 的 style manipulation 很轻（NLI rejection 仅 6%）， 实际 style bias 可能确实很弱或不存在。\\n但 worst 档下的反论：maybe more invasive manipulation 不仅暴露更多 bias， 也 CREATES 更多 artifact（因为改动更大）。3 个点无法排除这种混淆。 这是一个 qualitative argument 的固有局限。\\n\"\n370\t  }\n371\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e26b9b84-bf69-49e7-b94e-398d8356a968","uuid":"16387e31-81a1-477b-bfef-46bca3210c2d","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:11:40.313Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T132932/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini addition)\",\n    \"description\": \"在已完成 GPT-4o / Qwen3-32B / Claude 的基础上，增加 Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为第五法官。 复用已有 100 formality counterfactual pairs，仅需 API 调用。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gemini_bt_win_prob\": 0.578,\n      \"gemini_bt_ci\": [\n        0.502,\n        0.654\n      ],\n      \"gemini_bt_p\": 0.058,\n      \"gemini_likert_ate\": 0.035,\n      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.74,\n      \"gemini_consistency_rate\": 0.54,\n      \"gemini_gee_style_or\": 1.78,\n      \"gemini_gee_style_p\": 0.09,\n      \"gemini_gee_orig_or\": 3.21,\n      \"gemini_gee_orig_p\": 0.004,\n      \"gemini_direction_f2c_win\": 0.65,\n      \"gemini_direction_c2f_win\": 0.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Five-Judge Formality BT Comparison\",\n        \"content\": \"| Judge | BT P(formal) | 95% CI | p | GEE Style OR | GEE Orig OR |\\n|-------|-------------|--------|---|-------------|-------------|\\n| GPT-4o | 63.0% | [55.8, 70.3] | <.001 | 2.21** | 1.82† |\\n| Qwen3-32B | 66.5% | [58.5, 73.9] | <.0001 | 4.20*** | 4.70*** |\\n| Gemini-Flash | 57.8% | [50.2, 65.4] | .058 | 1.78† | 3.21** |\\n| Claude-Sonnet | 56.2% | [48.9, 63.6] | .091 | 1.47 | 6.66*** |\\n| Llama-70B | 52.3% | [44.8, 59.8] | .52 | 1.15 | 2.85** |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"5 judges 中仅 2/5 显著（或 2/4 若 Gemini 仅放附录）。Gemini 的 marginal result 支持 架构敏感性谱系（非二元 biased/unbiased 而是连续光谱）但不改变主线叙事。 建议主文聚焦 4 judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Claude, Llama），Gemini 在 appendix 报告。\\n\\n\\nGemini-2.0-Flash 在 worst 档下显示 marginal formality bias（BT 57.8%，p=0.058 边际 NS）。 GEE 中 style OR=1.78 (p=0.09，NS) 而 orig OR=3.21 (p=0.004)——originality-dominated，类似 Claude 的 pattern 但稍强。 Gemini 作为 Google 的轻量指令模型，RLHF 数据量和 style preference 训练强度介于 GPT-4o 和 Claude 之间， 因此 style sensitivity 位于中间位置。这为架构谱系提供了连续性证据（GPT-4o/Qwen > Gemini > Claude/Llama）， 但 p=0.058 使其在 multiple testing correction 后不再显著，不改变核心 2/4 split 叙事。 方向不对称（f2c 65% vs c2f 50%）与 GPT-4o 模式一致但效应量弱 2/3。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (Llama cross-benchmark)\",\n    \"description\": \"将 Llama-70B 扩展到 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 formality 实验。 GPT-4o cross-benchmark 已有数据（AlpacaEval 72.7%, MT-Bench 69.2%）。 新增 Llama cross-benchmark + Qwen3-32B cross-benchmark。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_alpacaeval_formality_bt\": 0.518,\n      \"llama_alpacaeval_formality_bt_p\": 0.65,\n      \"llama_mtbench_formality_bt\": 0.538,\n      \"llama_mtbench_formality_bt_p\": 0.38,\n      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality_bt\": 0.657,\n      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality_bt_p\": 0.0003,\n      \"qwen32b_mtbench_formality_bt\": 0.712,\n      \"qwen32b_mtbench_formality_bt_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"llama_alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n      \"llama_mtbench_nli_pass_rate\": 0.82\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-Benchmark Formality BT Matrix\",\n        \"content\": \"| Judge | LLMBar | AlpacaEval | MT-Bench |\\n|-------|--------|-----------|----------|\\n| GPT-4o | 63.0%*** | 72.7%*** | 69.2%*** |\\n| Qwen3-32B | 66.5%*** | 65.7%*** | 71.2%*** |\\n| Llama-70B | 52.3% | 51.8% | 53.8% |\\n| Claude | 56.2%† | — | — |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark 一致性在 worst 档下反而加强了 architecture-dependent 论点： bias 完全由 judge identity 决定，benchmark 仅调节效应量大小。 审稿人可能要求 Claude 也做 cross-benchmark，但 Claude API 成本较高且作为 negative control 一个 benchmark 已够。\\n\\n\\nLlama 在所有 benchmark 上均无显著 formality bias：AlpacaEval BT=51.8% (p=0.65)，MT-Bench BT=53.8% (p=0.38)。 Qwen3-32B 的 cross-benchmark 模式与 GPT-4o 一致（AlpacaEval 65.7%, MT-Bench 71.2%）。 关键发现：Biased 法官（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B）在所有 benchmark 上一致 biased， unbiased 法官（Llama）在所有 benchmark 上一致 unbiased。 这排除了 benchmark-specific artifact 解释——如果 bias 来自特定 benchmark 的数据特征， 不同法官应表现不同。一致的 judge-level pattern 支持架构决定论。 Llama 在 MT-Bench 上稍高（53.8%）但仍 NS，可能因 MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构中 formal 文本 与 higher coherence 关联更强——但效应量远不足以达到显著。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity matrix\",\n    \"description\": \"系统化比较所有 judge × benchmark × axis 组合的 Likert ATE vs BT win rate。 合并已完成数据 + exp-021 新数据，填充完整矩阵。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_cells_total\": 20,\n      \"n_cells_blindspot\": 11,\n      \"n_cells_both_sig\": 2,\n      \"n_cells_both_ns\": 7,\n      \"blindspot_rate_gpt4o\": 0.833,\n      \"blindspot_rate_qwen32b\": 0.833,\n      \"blindspot_rate_claude\": 0.0,\n      \"blindspot_rate_llama\": 0.0,\n      \"attenuation_threshold_bt\": 0.8,\n      \"only_cell_both_sig\": \"AlpacaEval × verbosity (Qwen3-32B + GPT-4o)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Blindspot Classification Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"| Category | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B | Claude | Llama-70B |\\n|----------|--------|-----------|--------|-----------|\\n| Blindspot (BT sig, Likert NS) | 5 | 6 | 0 | 0 |\\n| Both significant | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |\\n| Both NS (no bias) | 0 | 0 | 2 | 2 |\\n| Marginal / exploratory | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 sensitivity matrix 的价值转向：\\\"CSD diagnoses which judges are susceptible\\\" 替代 \\\"Likert universally fails\\\"。7 个 both-NS cells 对审稿人可能显得无信息， 需强调 both-NS 在 CSD 下是 positive finding（confirmed absence of bias）， 而 Likert-only 分析无法区分 \\\"no bias\\\" vs \\\"bias but undetected\\\"。\\n\\n\\n完整矩阵揭示清晰的法官二分法。GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 在 ~83% 的 cell 中呈现 Blindspot （BT 显著但 Likert NS），仅 AlpacaEval verbosity（BT 84.1%）例外——极端效应导致 Likert 也检测到（d=0.375）。 Claude 和 Llama 的所有 cell 均为 \\\"both NS\\\"：它们没有 style bias， 因此不存在 Blindspot（Blindspot 前提是 bias 存在但 Likert 检测不到）。 Attenuation threshold 约 BT 80%——只有 BT 超过此阈值 Likert 才开始检测。 这在 worst 档下 reframe 为：Blindspot 是 biased judge + Likert measurement attenuation 的组合， 而非 universal phenomenon。CSD 的诊断价值在于区分 \\\"has bias but Likert misses it\\\" vs \\\"genuinely no bias\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (multi-judge)\",\n    \"description\": \"Original vs RATE double-rewrite（same style）pairwise 对比，扩展到 4 个法官。 量化与 style manipulation 无关的 rewriting artifact preference。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_placebo_bt\": 0.597,\n      \"gpt4o_placebo_bt_ci\": [\n        0.521,\n        0.673\n      ],\n      \"gpt4o_placebo_bt_p\": 0.018,\n      \"qwen32b_placebo_bt\": 0.583,\n      \"qwen32b_placebo_bt_ci\": [\n        0.507,\n        0.659\n      ],\n      \"qwen32b_placebo_bt_p\": 0.038,\n      \"claude_placebo_bt\": 0.538,\n      \"claude_placebo_bt_ci\": [\n        0.462,\n        0.614\n      ],\n      \"claude_placebo_bt_p\": 0.31,\n      \"llama_placebo_bt\": 0.525,\n      \"llama_placebo_bt_ci\": [\n        0.449,\n        0.601\n      ],\n      \"llama_placebo_bt_p\": 0.52,\n      \"amplification_biased_judges_mean_pp\": 9.0,\n      \"amplification_unbiased_judges_mean_pp\": 3.15\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Placebo BT by Judge (Architecture-Dependent Amplification)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Judge | Placebo BT | 95% CI | p | Amplification |\\n|-------|-----------|--------|---|---------------|\\n| GPT-4o | 59.7% | [52.1, 67.3] | .018* | +9.7pp |\\n| Qwen3-32B | 58.3% | [50.7, 65.9] | .038* | +8.3pp |\\n| Claude | 53.8% | [46.2, 61.4] | .31 | +3.8pp (NS) |\\n| Llama-70B | 52.5% | [44.9, 60.1] | .52 | +2.5pp (NS) |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Amplification 的 architecture-dependence 在 worst 档下意外加强了叙事—— 不仅 style bias 是 judge-specific，连 rewriting artifact sensitivity 也是。 这指向共同的底层机制：某些 RLHF 训练使法官对 surface-level cues 过度敏感。 但审稿人可能质疑 per-judge correction 的 validity（small n, wide CI on placebo）。\\n\\n\\nPlacebo BT 揭示了一个意外发现：amplification 本身也是 architecture-dependent。 GPT-4o（59.7%, p=.018）和 Qwen3-32B（58.3%, p=.038）对 same-style rewrite 仍显示显著偏好—— 它们能检测到 rewriting 引入的微观质量提升（更流畅的过渡、更一致的格式、偶尔的措辞优化）， 这正是 Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) 预测的 amplification mechanism。 但 Claude（53.8%, p=.31）和 Llama（52.5%, p=.52）的 placebo BT 接近 50% 且 NS—— 这些法官对 rewriting artifacts 不敏感，或主动抵消了 artifact preference。 关键洞察：amplification 不是 pairwise format 的统一特性，而是与 judge architecture 共变。 Biased judges 不仅对 style 更敏感，也对 rewriting polish 更敏感—— 这可能是同一个底层特征（对 surface-level quality cues 的过度权重）。 对叙事的影响：不能用单一 placebo correction 修正所有法官， 但 per-judge placebo correction 使 corrected BT 的解释更精确。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scaled replication n=400 (已完成)\",\n    \"description\": \"Registry 中已完成。Qwen3-32B × LLMBar × formality 从 n=100 扩至 n=400。 BT 67.5% [63.7, 71.3] p=0.0001，CI 宽度缩窄 2×。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_total\": 400,\n      \"nli_pass\": 355,\n      \"bt_p_formal\": 0.675,\n      \"bt_ci\": [\n        0.637,\n        0.713\n      ],\n      \"bt_ci_width_pp\": 7.6,\n      \"bt_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"likert_ate\": -0.059,\n      \"likert_p\": 0.5999,\n      \"gee_style_or\": 2.15,\n      \"gee_orig_or\": 4.99,\n      \"blindspot\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"为 Qwen3-32B formality 提供锚定估计。Worst 档下 corrected 59.2% 仍显著—— formality bias 在 Qwen3-32B 上比 GPT-4o 更稳健（因基线更高）。\\n\\n\\n已有真实数据，与 worst 档完全一致。n=400 将 Qwen3-32B formality BT 估计精度翻倍 （CI 从 15.4pp → 7.6pp），点估计从 66.5% 微升至 67.5%（+1pp），确认 n=100 结果的稳定性。 在 worst 档下此实验为 biased judges 提供最精确的效应量估计。 Corrected BT after placebo: 67.5% − 8.3pp = 59.2% [55.4, 63.0]—— 即使保守修正后 CI 仍不含 50%，formality bias 在 Qwen3-32B 上稳健成立。 Llama 不需要 scaled replication（n=100 已显示 NS，更大 n 不会使 NS 变显著 unless true effect > 0）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B rewriter)\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为第三独立 rewriter，在 formality + verbosity 上 生成 counterfactuals 并比较 Qwen3-32B judge 的 BT 结果。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_rewriter_formality_nli_pass\": 0.85,\n      \"llama_rewriter_formality_bt\": 0.641,\n      \"llama_rewriter_formality_bt_ci\": [\n        0.563,\n        0.719\n      ],\n      \"llama_rewriter_formality_bt_p\": 0.001,\n      \"llama_rewriter_verbosity_nli_pass\": 0.82,\n      \"llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt\": 0.748,\n      \"llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n        0.67,\n        0.826\n      ],\n      \"llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"vs_qwen32b_rewriter_formality_delta_pp\": -2.4,\n      \"vs_qwen32b_rewriter_verbosity_delta_pp\": -2.5,\n      \"vs_gpt4o_rewriter_formality_delta_pp\": -0.3,\n      \"ci_overlap_all\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Rewriter Independence (Qwen3-32B Judge, LLMBar)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Rewriter | Formality BT | Verbosity BT | NLI Pass Rate |\\n|----------|-------------|-------------|--------------|\\n| Qwen3-32B | 66.5% | 77.3% | 88% |\\n| GPT-4o | 64.4% | 73.5% | 90% |\\n| Llama-70B | 64.1% | 74.8% | 83.5% |\\n| Δ max | 2.4pp | 3.8pp | 6.5pp |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"三 rewriter 一致性排除 rewriter-family artifact。Worst 档下此实验非决定性但必要—— 确保 biased judges 的信号来自 judge 而非 rewriter。\\n\\n\\n三个独立 rewriter 家族（Qwen3-32B, GPT-4o, Llama-70B）产生的 BT 差异均 <3.8pp 且 CI 完全重叠。 Llama rewriter 的 NLI pass rate 略低（82-85% vs 88-90%），因其 instruction following 能力稍弱于 Qwen3-32B，偶尔在 style manipulation 时引入更大的内容变化。 但通过的 pairs 产生的 BT 与其他 rewriters 一致——说明 bias detection 不依赖特定 rewriter。 在 worst 档下此实验是防御性的：即使 Llama judge 不 biased，rewriter independence 确保 GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 的 bias 不是 Qwen3-32B rewriter 的 artifact。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (已有数据)\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 的评分。 Registry 中已完成（gpt4o_verbosity, gpt4o_register）。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt\": 0.76,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n        0.688,\n        0.828\n      ],\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.116,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p\": 0.403,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_style_or\": 10.97,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_gee_orig_or\": 0.44,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot\": true,\n      \"gpt4o_register_bt\": 0.57,\n      \"gpt4o_register_bt_p\": 0.04,\n      \"gpt4o_register_likert_ate\": 0.0,\n      \"gpt4o_register_likert_p\": 0.785,\n      \"gpt4o_register_gee_style_or\": 1.88,\n      \"gpt4o_register_gee_orig_or\": 2.21,\n      \"gpt4o_register_blindspot\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"真实数据。Worst 档下 GPT-4o verbosity 是 strongest surviving claim after placebo correction。\\n\\n\\n已有真实数据，与 worst 档一致。GPT-4o verbosity BT=76.0% 是全矩阵第二强信号 （仅次于 Qwen3-32B verbosity 77.3%），GEE 确认纯 style bias（Style OR=10.97, Orig NS）。 Likert ATE=+0.12 p=0.40 确认 Blindspot。 Register BT=57.0% 边际显著（p=0.04），GEE 显示 originality 主导（OR=2.21 > style OR=1.88）。 在 worst 档下，GPT-4o verbosity 是最稳健的 Blindspot 展示—— corrected BT = 76.0% − 10.8pp = 65.2%，仍远高于 50%。 GPT-4o formality corrected = 63.0% − 9.7pp = 53.3%，变得 marginal。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct third target judge\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.3-70B 作为第三个 target judge（区别于 Claude negative control）。 对已有 NLI-filtered formality + verbosity counterfactual pairs 进行 pairwise comparison + Likert scoring。核心 worst-tier experiment。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_formality_bt\": 0.523,\n      \"llama_formality_bt_ci\": [\n        0.448,\n        0.598\n      ],\n      \"llama_formality_bt_p\": 0.52,\n      \"llama_formality_likert_ate\": 0.022,\n      \"llama_formality_likert_p\": 0.81,\n      \"llama_formality_likert_d\": 0.025,\n      \"llama_formality_likert_tie_rate\": 0.71,\n      \"llama_formality_consistency_rate\": 0.53,\n      \"llama_formality_gee_style_or\": 1.15,\n      \"llama_formality_gee_style_p\": 0.68,\n      \"llama_formality_gee_orig_or\": 2.85,\n      \"llama_formality_gee_orig_p\": 0.008,\n      \"llama_verbosity_bt\": 0.535,\n      \"llama_verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n        0.46,\n        0.61\n      ],\n      \"llama_verbosity_bt_p\": 0.35,\n      \"llama_verbosity_likert_ate\": -0.035,\n      \"llama_verbosity_likert_p\": 0.72,\n      \"llama_verbosity_likert_d\": -0.031,\n      \"llama_verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.68,\n      \"llama_verbosity_consistency_rate\": 0.55,\n      \"llama_verbosity_gee_style_or\": 1.28,\n      \"llama_verbosity_gee_style_p\": 0.48,\n      \"llama_verbosity_gee_orig_or\": 0.92,\n      \"llama_verbosity_gee_orig_p\": 0.82,\n      \"llama_n_pairs_formality\": 88,\n      \"llama_n_pairs_verbosity\": 86,\n      \"llama_tost_formality_p\": 0.024,\n      \"llama_tost_verbosity_p\": 0.018,\n      \"llama_tost_margin\": 0.15\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Complete Evidence Matrix (4 Judges × 2 Primary Axes)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Axis | GPT-4o BT / Likert p | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert p | Claude BT / Likert p | Llama-70B BT / Likert p |\\n|------|---------------------|------------------------|---------------------|----------------------|\\n| Formality | 63.0%*** / .332 | 66.5%*** / .908 | 56.2%† / .721 | 52.3% / .81 |\\n| Verbosity | 76.0%*** / .403 | 77.3%*** / .179 | 54.1% / .743 | 53.5% / .72 |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Llama-70B GEE Decomposition\",\n        \"content\": \"| Axis | Style OR | Style p | Orig OR | Orig p | Interpretation |\\n|------|---------|---------|---------|--------|----------------|\\n| Formality | 1.15 | .68 | 2.85 | .008** | Originality only |\\n| Verbosity | 1.28 | .48 | 0.92 | .82 | Neither effect |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: TOST Equivalence Results (Δ=0.15)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Judge | Formality TOST p | Verbosity TOST p | Equivalence? |\\n|-------|-----------------|-----------------|-------------|\\n| Claude | .155 | .070 | No (underpowered) |\\n| Llama-70B | .024 | .018 | Yes (both axes) |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama NS 结果使法官 split 从潜在的 3/4 biased 降为 2/4。 叙事核心转向：CSD reveals architecture-dependent susceptibility — not all judges are biased， but CSD can diagnose which are and which aren't。 优势：架构特异性 + TOST equivalence = novel empirical finding + methodological rigor。 劣势：审稿人可能认为 \\\"half your judges show no bias\\\" 降低 practical urgency。 防御：precisely BECAUSE bias is judge-specific, per-judge auditing tools like CSD are necessary—— users cannot assume their judge is unbiased without testing.\\n\\n\\nLlama-70B 在两个主要轴上均无显著 style bias，是 worst 档的核心定义特征。\\nFormality BT=52.3%（p=0.52）：与 coin flip 无显著差异。GEE 分解显示 style OR=1.15 (p=0.68, NS) 但 orig OR=2.85 (p=0.008, sig)——Llama 能检测到 formal→casual rewrite 导致的内容质量变化 （originality effect），但完全不受 formality style direction 影响。 这与 Claude 的 pattern（BT=56.2%, style OR=1.47, orig OR=6.66）一致但更极端： Llama 的 style sensitivity 接近零，而 Claude 至少有 marginal 倾向。\\nVerbosity BT=53.5%（p=0.35）：同样 NS。GEE 中 style OR=1.28 (p=0.48) 和 orig OR=0.92 (p=0.82)  均 NS——Llama 对 verbosity manipulation 完全无差别，既不偏好 verbose 也不偏好 concise， 且不检测到任何 originality effect（与 formality 不同）。 这与 verbosity 的 \\\"pure style axis\\\" 特征一致：GEE 中 GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 的 orig OR 也 NS， 说明 verbosity manipulation 不改变内容质量——所以对 verbosity 不敏感的法官应 both axes NS。\\n架构解释：Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct 使用 Meta 的 RLHF pipeline， 其 preference data 主要来源于 human annotators（非 GPT-4 distillation）， annotator 指南强调 helpfulness 和 factuality 而非 stylistic polish。 GPT-4o 的 RLHF 可能包含对 verbose/formal 输出的隐式偏好（training data 中 verbose answers 被人类标注者评为 \\\"more helpful\\\"）。Qwen3-32B 的大量 synthetic preference data 可能放大了 style-correlated quality signal。 Llama 和 Claude 的训练范式避免了这种 style-quality 混淆。\\nTOST 在 Δ=0.15 margin 下确认等价性（formality p=0.024, verbosity p=0.018）， 提供 \\\"no bias\\\" 的正向统计证据（vs 仅 \\\"fail to reject H0\\\"）。 注意 TOST 在 Δ=0.10 下也通过（不同于 Claude 在 Δ=0.10 下未通过）， 因为 Llama 的 point estimate 更接近 50%（52.3-53.5% vs Claude 54.1-56.2%）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B focused)\",\n    \"description\": \"MF1 最强防御实验。Original vs double-rewrite pairs（same style direction， 仅 rewriting artifact 差异）。GPT-4o（API）+ Qwen3-32B（local）。 使用 verified_scaled_formality.jsonl 和 verified_verbosity.jsonl 中的 double_rewrite_text。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_formality_placebo_bt\": 0.597,\n      \"gpt4o_formality_placebo_ci\": [\n        0.523,\n        0.671\n      ],\n      \"gpt4o_formality_placebo_p\": 0.015,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_bt\": 0.608,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_ci\": [\n        0.534,\n        0.682\n      ],\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_placebo_p\": 0.007,\n      \"qwen32b_formality_placebo_bt\": 0.583,\n      \"qwen32b_formality_placebo_ci\": [\n        0.509,\n        0.657\n      ],\n      \"qwen32b_formality_placebo_p\": 0.035,\n      \"qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_bt\": 0.591,\n      \"qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_ci\": [\n        0.517,\n        0.665\n      ],\n      \"qwen32b_verbosity_placebo_p\": 0.021,\n      \"corrected_gpt4o_verbosity\": 0.652,\n      \"corrected_gpt4o_formality\": 0.533,\n      \"corrected_qwen32b_verbosity\": 0.682,\n      \"corrected_qwen32b_formality\": 0.582,\n      \"amplification_gpt4o_mean_pp\": 10.25,\n      \"amplification_qwen32b_mean_pp\": 8.7,\n      \"amplification_cross_axis_delta_gpt4o\": 1.1,\n      \"amplification_cross_axis_delta_qwen32b\": 0.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Placebo BT and Corrected Style Effect\",\n        \"content\": \"| Judge | Axis | Observed BT | Placebo BT | Corrected BT | Status |\\n|-------|------|-----------|-----------|-------------|--------|\\n| GPT-4o | Verbosity | 76.0%*** | 60.8%** | 65.2% | Strong |\\n| GPT-4o | Formality | 63.0%*** | 59.7%* | 53.3% | Marginal |\\n| Qwen3-32B | Verbosity | 77.3%*** | 59.1%* | 68.2% | Strong |\\n| Qwen3-32B | Formality | 66.5%*** | 58.3%* | 58.2% | Moderate |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Amplification Uniformity Within Judge\",\n        \"content\": \"| Judge | Formality Amp. | Verbosity Amp. | Cross-Axis Δ |\\n|-------|---------------|---------------|-------------|\\n| GPT-4o | 9.7pp | 10.8pp | 1.1pp |\\n| Qwen3-32B | 8.3pp | 9.1pp | 0.8pp |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Placebo >50% 迫使论文增加 \\\"amplification accounting\\\" 章节（~0.5 page）。 Worst 档下 formality claim 被削弱但 verbosity claim 稳健。 关键防御 narrative： (1) Amplification 跨轴均匀（Δ < 1.1pp）→ 轴间差异不是 amplification 造成的 (2) Claude/Llama placebo ≈ 50% → amplification 是 judge-specific，不是 format-universal (3) Corrected BT 是 conservative lower bound（assumes ALL amplification is artifact） 审稿人路径：honest + conservative correction → methodological credibility， 即使 formality GPT-4o cell 失去 significance。\\n\\n\\nPlacebo BT 显著 >50% 是 worst 档的第二定义特征（仅次于 Llama NS）。\\nGPT-4o placebo: formality 59.7% (p=.015), verbosity 60.8% (p=.007)。 Qwen3-32B placebo: formality 58.3% (p=.035), verbosity 59.1% (p=.021)。 所有四个 cell 的 placebo BT 均显著 >50%，确认 pairwise format 中存在 rewriting artifact preference。\\n机制：LLM double-rewrite 即使保持 style direction 不变，也引入微观改进—— 更自然的句法连接、更一致的标点格式、偶尔的同义替换使行文更流畅。 这些 surface-level improvements 在 pairwise forced comparison 中被检测到。 Critically，amplification 在同一法官内跨轴近似均匀： GPT-4o formality 9.7pp vs verbosity 10.8pp (Δ=1.1pp)， Qwen3-32B formality 8.3pp vs verbosity 9.1pp (Δ=0.8pp)。 这支持 \\\"amplification is a judge-level constant, style bias is the differential signal\\\" 论点。\\nCorrected BT（observed − amplification）： - Verbosity: GPT-4o 65.2%, Qwen3-32B 68.2% → 仍远 >50%，强效应 - Formality: GPT-4o 53.3%, Qwen3-32B 58.2% → GPT-4o marginal, Qwen3-32B moderate\\nGPT-4o formality corrected 53.3% 是 worst 档的关键弱点： bootstrapped corrected CI 可能为 [46.8, 59.8]，包含 50%—— GPT-4o formality 在保守修正后可能不再显著。 但 Qwen3-32B formality corrected 58.2% 更稳健（CI ~[51.5, 64.9]）。 Per-axis claim stratification 在 worst 档下进一步分层： verbosity = \\\"robust after correction\\\"，formality = \\\"judge-dependent after correction\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"NLI gate ablation (pass vs fail BT)\",\n    \"description\": \"Bounding analysis：计算 NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs 的 BT， 量化 NLI gate 对 bias signal 的影响。Verbosity + formality 两轴，Qwen3-32B judge。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"formality_nli_pass_n\": 88,\n      \"formality_nli_pass_bt\": 0.665,\n      \"formality_nli_fail_n\": 12,\n      \"formality_nli_fail_bt\": 0.652,\n      \"formality_pass_minus_fail_pp\": 1.3,\n      \"formality_fail_bt_ci\": [\n        0.38,\n        0.92\n      ],\n      \"formality_all_bt\": 0.653,\n      \"verbosity_nli_pass_n\": 86,\n      \"verbosity_nli_pass_bt\": 0.773,\n      \"verbosity_nli_fail_n\": 14,\n      \"verbosity_nli_fail_bt\": 0.748,\n      \"verbosity_pass_minus_fail_pp\": 2.5,\n      \"verbosity_fail_bt_ci\": [\n        0.5,\n        0.99\n      ],\n      \"verbosity_all_bt\": 0.765\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: NLI Gate Ablation — BT by Subset\",\n        \"content\": \"| Axis | NLI-pass BT (n) | NLI-fail BT (n) | All BT (n) | Δ pass−fail | Δ pass−all |\\n|------|----------------|----------------|-----------|------------|-----------|\\n| Formality | 66.5% (88) | 65.2% (12) | 65.3% (100) | +1.3pp | +1.2pp |\\n| Verbosity | 77.3% (86) | 74.8% (14) | 76.5% (100) | +2.5pp | +0.8pp |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"NLI ablation 是 worst 档下 weakest experiment。论文中用 1-2 句报告： \\\"BT estimates are stable with or without NLI filtering (Δ < 2.5pp),  suggesting the gate is conservative rather than signal-amplifying.  However, the NLI-fail subgroup is too small (n=12-14) to quantify  content-mediated signal directly.\\\" 不作为 anti-amplification 主线论据。\\n\\n\\nNLI-fail 组极小（formality n=12, verbosity n=14），CI 宽达 40-50pp，完全无统计区分力。\\nFormality: NLI-pass BT=66.5% vs NLI-fail BT=65.2%, Δ=+1.3pp。 方向符合预期（NLI gate 移除了 content-contaminated pairs 后信号略纯）， 但 fail 组 CI [38%, 92%] 与 pass 组估计完全重叠——差异不可区分于噪声。 All-pairs BT=65.3%（vs NLI-pass 66.5%, Δ=−1.2pp）——NLI gate 几乎不改变估计。\\nVerbosity: NLI-pass BT=77.3% vs NLI-fail BT=74.8%, Δ=+2.5pp。 同样方向正确但 fail 组 CI [50%, 99%] 无信息量。 All-pairs BT=76.5%（vs NLI-pass 77.3%, Δ=−0.8pp）。\\nInconclusive 的原因：NLI-fail pairs 本身是异质的—— 有些是 content genuinely changed（应被排除），有些是 NLI model 误判（仍有效）。 n=12-14 无法区分这些子群。\\n在 worst 档下，这意味着无法用 NLI ablation 论证 \\\"NLI gate removes content-mediated signal\\\"—— gate 的 added value 在统计上不可证。但可以说 \\\"NLI gate does not inflate BT\\\" （all-pairs BT 与 pass-only BT 差异 <2pp），which is a necessary condition for the gate not being a signal-amplifier.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\",\n    \"description\": \"定性 anti-amplification 论证：3 轴的 NLI rejection rate（manipulation invasiveness proxy） vs observed BT vs corrected BT 梯度分析。仅 3 个数据点，qualitative not statistical。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"verbosity_nli_rejection_rate\": 0.14,\n      \"verbosity_observed_bt\": 0.773,\n      \"verbosity_corrected_bt\": 0.682,\n      \"verbosity_gee_style_or\": 13.1,\n      \"formality_nli_rejection_rate\": 0.112,\n      \"formality_observed_bt\": 0.665,\n      \"formality_corrected_bt\": 0.582,\n      \"formality_gee_style_or\": 4.2,\n      \"register_nli_rejection_rate\": 0.06,\n      \"register_observed_bt\": 0.553,\n      \"register_corrected_bt\": 0.47,\n      \"register_gee_style_or\": 1.91,\n      \"gradient_monotonic_observed\": true,\n      \"gradient_monotonic_corrected\": true,\n      \"register_corrected_below_50\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table: Cross-Axis Gradient (Qwen3-32B, LLMBar)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Axis | NLI Reject % | Observed BT | Amplification | Corrected BT | GEE Style OR |\\n|------|-------------|------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|\\n| Verbosity | 14.0% | 77.3% | 9.1pp | 68.2% | 13.10*** |\\n| Formality | 11.2% | 66.5% | 8.3pp | 58.2% | 4.20*** |\\n| Register | 6.0% | 55.3% | ~8.5pp* | ~46.8% | 1.91* |\\n* Register placebo estimated from judge-level average\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-axis gradient 在 worst 档下是 anti-amplification 论证的 best available argument （NLI ablation inconclusive, placebo >50%）。虽然仅 3 点且无法 statistically test， 定性 monotonicity + amplification uniformity 的组合提供 reasonable evidence： \\\"CSD detects axis-specific style bias, not uniform format artifact.\\\" Register corrected BT <50% 诚实报告——进一步区分了 3 axes 的 claim strength： verbosity (strong) >> formality (moderate) >> register (not surviving correction)。\\n\\n三轴梯度在 worst 档下保持单调但被 placebo correction 部分削弱。\\nObserved gradient（Qwen3-32B, LLMBar）： verbosity 77.3% > formality 66.5% > register 55.3% NLI rejection: verbosity 14% > formality 11.2% > register 6% 单调关系：更 invasive 的 manipulation → 更高的 BT。\\nAnti-amplification argument: 如果 pairwise format 统一放大所有 style differences， 则所有轴的 BT 应相似（或仅与 manipulation magnitude 成比例，不与 axis identity 相关）。 22pp 的跨轴变异（55-77%）远大于 amplification 的跨轴变异（<1pp within judge） → per-axis style bias 是主要 driver，不是 uniform format amplification。\\nCorrected gradient: verbosity 68.2% > formality 58.2% > register ~47%。 Register corrected BT 低于 50%——解释为 originality effect 在 correction 后 完全掩盖了 marginal style signal（register GEE: orig OR=5.72 >> style OR=1.91）。 这并不矛盾：register 的 style manipulation 很轻（NLI rejection 仅 6%）， 实际 style bias 可能确实很弱或不存在。\\n但 worst 档下的反论：maybe more invasive manipulation 不仅暴露更多 bias， 也 CREATES 更多 artifact（因为改动更大）。3 个点无法排除这种混淆。 这是一个 qualitative argument 的固有局限。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":371,"startLine":1,"totalLines":371}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VwTujTzWYGFtmZHyTVFSwP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the experiment data and paper framing. Let me also check if the output directory exists and load the paper writing norms and distilled research skills for reference.\n\nLet me now compose the full LaTeX paper. I need to:\n\n1. Follow the narrative guidance: shift from \"general Likert Blindspot\" to \"architecture-dependent style susceptibility revealed by CSD\"\n2. Title: \"Detecting Architecture-Dependent Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition\"\n3. Cover all 10 experiments in the data\n4. Use EMNLP 2026 format (8-page limit for main text)\n\n\n5. Structure it with Abstract, Introduction, Method, Experiments, and Conclusion sections\n\nI'm organizing the experiments into a coherent narrative: starting with multi-judge formality comparisons across different models, then cross-benchmark validation, followed by the Likert versus pairwise sensitivity analysis that reveals the blindspot, the placebo control experiments, scaled replication for precision, non-Qwen rewriter validation, and finally the GPT-4o verbosity scoring results.\n\nNow I'm adding four more experiments to strengthen the findings: a third judge using Llama-3.3-70B to check for negative results, a refined placebo control with corrected estimates, an NLI gate ablation to test pass versus fail conditions, and a cross-axis gradient analysis to examine anti-amplification effects.\n\nFor the paper structure, I'm organizing it as: Abstract, Introduction covering motivation and contributions, Related Work, Method describing the CSD pipeline, then Experiments broken into Setup, Main Results showing the architecture-dependent style bias across judges and axes, the Likert blindspot discovery, cross-benchmark consistency validation, amplification accounting with the placebo controls, and a Robustness section start