{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014D7yxuLTkzwYLUzSnN3YRH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n2\t\n3\t\\usepackage[review]{acl}\n4\t\n5\t\\usepackage{times}\n6\t\\usepackage{latexsym}\n7\t\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n8\t\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n9\t\\usepackage{microtype}\n10\t\\usepackage{graphicx}\n11\t\\usepackage{booktabs}\n12\t\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}\n13\t\\usepackage{xcolor}\n14\t\\usepackage{multirow}\n15\t\\usepackage{array}\n16\t\n17\t\\title{The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias\\\\in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition}\n18\t\n19\t\\author{Anonymous}\n20\t\n21\t\\begin{document}\n22\t\\maketitle\n23\t\n24\t\\begin{abstract}\n25\tLLM-as-judge evaluation is increasingly central to NLP benchmarking and alignment, yet style biases---systematic preferences for superficial textual properties like verbosity or formality---can silently corrupt scores."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e26b9b84-bf69-49e7-b94e-398d8356a968","uuid":"24d63aed-1681-400b-a90f-ba5f73072f7b","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:12:12.048Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T132932/best/paper.tex","content":"\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage[review]{acl}\n\n\\usepackage{times}\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{microtype}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}\n\\usepackage{xcolor}\n\\usepackage{multirow}\n\\usepackage{array}\n\n\\title{The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias\\\\in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition}\n\n\\author{Anonymous}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nLLM-as-judge evaluation is increasingly central to NLP benchmarking and alignment, yet style biases---systematic preferences fo